.Dd June 17, 2026
.Dt BLUECTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bluectl
.Nd command-line client for the blued Bluetooth daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility communicates with the
.Xr blued 8
daemon via its Unix domain control socket.
It sends a command and prints the response to standard output.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s Ar socket
Path to the
.Xr blued 8
control socket.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/blued.sock .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "disconnect"
.It Cm scan
Start a Bluetooth Low Energy scan and print discovered devices.
Each result line includes the device address, address type, RSSI, and
name if available.
.It Cm list
List currently connected devices with their state and connection handle.
.It Cm adapters
List active Bluetooth adapters with their names and addresses.
.It Cm status
Print a single-line daemon status summary showing the number of active
adapters and connections.
.It Cm connect Ar addr Op Cm public | Cm random
Initiate a connection to the device with the specified Bluetooth address.
The optional address type may be
.Cm public
or
.Cm random ;
the default is
.Cm public .
.It Cm disconnect Ar addr
Disconnect the device with the specified Bluetooth address.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success, 1 if the daemon reported an error or the connection
to the control socket failed, and 2 (EX_USAGE) on invalid usage.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/blued.sock" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/blued.sock
Default control socket path.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr blued 8 ,
.Xr bluetooth 3
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
